 we leave without a deal and my  view is both options are extreme and  there is no mandate for either option  and so for a new prime minister to talk  either way without going back to the  people would be impossible that is why I  stood on platform of a referendum  because I wanted what I desperately want  one but we need a way to break the  impasse in a general election for the  Conservative Party at this stage would  be some of tomorrow so if if we get to  the end of October and the prime  minister who  is going to try and take the UK out the  EU without a deal will you try and stop  me  I have always voted against No Deal and  I will continue to do so and not just me  I think there are a lot of MPs on the  conservative side how many do you think  and cross Anna Collins well I think  there is a significant number and that  will vote that would use legislative  options to do two things I mean it's  that like less than 10 is that more like  30 I mean about 30 30 plus but what  we'll be looking to do is stop the new  prime minister from perogy in Parliament  in order to deliver a deal but also  create options for the new prime  minister so that new deal is not the  only option we face on the 31st of  October so how are you do that then well  there are there are a number of our  legislative mechanisms being looked at  at the moment and we will sort of come  to them when we do I wouldn't want sort  of announced them before you know they  may be self tested as viable but there  is a real concern and the real concern  here is not about levers or Romania's  the real concern here is that this is  not in the interest of our country now  in the last week you asked me what do I  think of the contest we've had a lot of  commentary on brexit and how we're going  to receive a brexit boost by cutting  this tax and cutting that tax actually  what all of this is about is Stephen of  economic mayhem now in a scenario where  you sort of break of your legs and get  on crutches and say that is a dividend  it's not a mobility dividend it's not  any different you know we already hurt  in the economy I think that is something  that most people are concerned about the  Union is also very important is een for  example Boris Johnson said he'll be  Minister for the Union but when you  reflect on it the imposing on the  Singlish Tories imposing on the Scots  the policy the least like and that  causes them harm is their most likely  way for us to have a second successful  Scottish independence referendum so no  deal could break up the country then  also harm our economy so for that reason  there are a lot of MPs and it's not  about leave remain who think that the  truly patriotic thing to do is not to  play to Nigel Farage's tune but to find  a better way for you  talking about some important issues  there but isn't democracy also important  the majority of people in the UK voted  to leave the European Union I mean that  is why we are here and if they feel that  MPs are effectively trying to ignore  them then that's going to be also mayhem  isn't it that's oh that's a complete  fallacy in the debate people voted to  leave the EU but people were told that  there will be a deal they leave campaign  to people that might be a deal if  someone is beta denied your Farraj and  those people didn't want that to you  right they say they don't want the deal  that's on the table but people were told  during a referendum campaign that there  will be a deal people were told in our  manifesto that there will be a deal  the anti-democratic thing to do would be  having promised people that there will  be a deal and they all have the exact  same benefits to take the EU the UK out  of the EU without a deal where people's  jobs suffer that is the undemocratic  thing to do in this situation nobody  voted to leave without a deal you were  clearly very worried about the idea of  leaving without a deal now early on the  programme Labour's Barry Gardner said  that Labour will hold a confidence  motion in the government when they fail  that there's enough support from the  conservative side can you rule out ever  voting against a Conservative government  in a confidence motion I've been very  explicit about that's not something I  intend to do you know I think it's the  nuclear option I don't want to go there  I know some that are considering it but  I wouldn't go there but I believe that  the measures come out yes but the other  measures we are looking at will be  sensible and will be pragmatic and will  create space for the new prime minister  to move away from what they think they  have to say in an election campaign for  160,000 members I mean you and governor  in the interests of the country you're  clearly talking to some of the MPs who  as you say potentially considering the  conference motion option do you think  there's enough that it might pass I  can't comment for others but but I think  that for the future of the many people  who think going leaving without a deal  and play to Nigel Farage's tune is a  good thing I think that is the way to  save the Conservative Party and I think  that is also wrong because the  Conservative Party that breaks up the  union a Conservative Party that damages  the economy but a Conservative Party  that becomes the governing arm of the  brexit party will very quickly  run out of voters and wouldn't be in  government very long would you say it's  an MP if you felt that was the case  oh yes I'm going to fight for what is  real conservatism and real conservative  is pragmatic real conservatism  is not worried about thinking again a  real conservatism above all puts the  country first and I think that is what I  in a number of my colleagues who are  concerned about New Deal will be  fighting for over the next few weeks and  months we want to rediscover what is may  the conservative party there was  successful Democratic Party in the world  is that we are pragmatic we're  pro-business and also we have been  instrumental to this 300 years  successful Union that our country us  that's what I'll be fighting for okay  Sam Chima thank you very much for coming  on the program this morning

